\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The limit set of a point that returns}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Take a state #{x} on a [closed orbit](fnip-0052), and let #{T>0} be
a time at which the solution through #{x} returns to #{x}. The times
#{kT}, as the integer #{k} runs through the positive integers, tend
to #{+\infty}, and the state is #{x} at each of them, so #{x} lies in
its own [omega-limit set](fnip-0052). The same times with #{k}
negative tend to #{-\infty}, so #{x} lies in its own
[alpha-limit set](fnip-0052). Every other state on the orbit arises
in the same way, and the orbit stays in both limit sets.}

\p{The omega-limit set of an [equilibrium](fnip-0014) is the
equilibrium itself. The constant solution is there at every time.}
